 "cells": [
  {
   "file": "cells/intro.json",
   "id": "intro",
   "kind": "markdown",
   "markdown": "# Resonance\n\nPush the [damped oscillator](oscillator.jl) with a periodic force of frequency ``\\Omega``, measured in\nunits of its natural frequency, and once the start-up transient has died away it oscillates at the\ndriving frequency. How far it swings depends on how close ``\\Omega`` is to 1, and on the damping ratio\n``\\zeta``: the same ``\\zeta`` that sets how quickly [its free oscillation decays](oscillator.jl#peaks).\n\n\n\n```math\nA(\\Omega) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(1-\\Omega^2)^2 + (2\\zeta\\Omega)^2}}\n```\n\n",
   "native": true,
   "output": true,
   "tags": []
  },
  {
   "file": "cells/controls.json",
   "hidecode": true,
   "id": "controls",
   "kind": "code",
   "output": true,
   "source": "@bind zeta Slider(0.05:0.05:1.0; default = 0.1)",
   "tags": []
  },
  {
   "hidecode": false,
   "id": "model",
   "kind": "code",
   "output": false,
   "source": "A(Ω, ζ) = 1 / sqrt((1 - Ω^2)^2 + (2ζ * Ω)^2)\nΩs = collect(range(0, 3; length = 300))\nΩpeak = zeta < 1 / sqrt(2) ? sqrt(1 - 2zeta^2) : 0.0\nnothing",
   "tags": []
  },
  {
   "file": "cells/peak_md.json",
   "id": "peak_md",
   "kind": "markdown",
   "markdown": "At ζ = 0.1 the response peaks at Ω = 0.99, where the oscillator swings\n5.03 times as far as the same force would push it if applied steadily.",
   "native": false,
   "output": true,
   "tags": []
  },
  {
   "file": "cells/response.json",
   "hidecode": false,
   "id": "response",
   "kind": "code",
   "output": true,
   "source": "echart(:line, Ωs, @replay(zeta, [A(Ω, zeta) for Ω in Ωs]);\n       name = \"A(Ω)\", showSymbol = false,\n       xAxis = (type = :value, name = \"Ω\"), yAxis = (type = :log, name = \"amplitude\"))",
   "tags": [
    "macrocall"
   ]
  },
  {
   "file": "cells/q_md.json",
   "id": "q_md",
   "kind": "markdown",
   "markdown": "## Quality factor\n\nLight damping gives a tall, narrow peak. Its sharpness is the quality factor ``Q = 1/(2\\zeta)``, which\nfor light damping is also roughly the number of cycles the [free oscillation](oscillator.jl) takes to\nlose most of its energy.",
   "native": true,
   "output": true,
   "tags": []
  },
  {
   "file": "cells/qtable.json",
   "hidecode": false,
   "id": "qtable",
   "kind": "code",
   "output": true,
   "source": "slate_table([(ζ = z, Q = round(1 / (2z); digits = 2), peak = round(A(sqrt(max(1 - 2z^2, 0.0)), z); digits = 2))\n             for z in (0.02, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.5)])",
   "tags": []
  }
 ],
